<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is MAM Auditer and why is it required?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"MAM Auditer is our structured entry assessment system. It measures 10 dimensions — rhythm intelligence, ear sensitivity, performance confidence, technical knowledge, artistic potential, discipline and learning capacity — so we place you in the right pathway from day one. Students are not randomly placed; they are intelligently assessed."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I study online or do I have to come to Lagos?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"All MAM programmes are offered in two modes. Online: live video classes, online coaching, digital assignments, virtual rehearsals — from anywhere. Onsite: in-person at MAM Centre, Lagos — for practical rehearsals, ensemble training, live stagecraft and group interactions."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How are MAM certifications equivalent to Trinity London?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Our four pathways map directly to Trinity College London grade bands: Pre-Certification (Grade 1–2), Certification (Grade 3–4), Pre-Diploma (Grade 5–6) and Diploma (Grade 7–8). Plus the MAM Method adds rhythm intelligence, performance intelligence and creative consciousness on top."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does each pathway cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Certified Musician from $240 (one tradition) · Grand Musician from $313 (all three traditions, 13% off), both spanning all four certification levels and available online or onsite. Registration is $5 (one-time). Crash Programmes are a flat $70 for a 6-week accelerated intensive. The MetaMusic Order (12 weeks) is $60."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is The MetaMusic Order?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A 12-week civilization-engineering intensive that moves musicians from Performer → Architect. It immerses students in sound psychology, cultural engineering, atmosphere architecture, performance intelligence and national responsibility. Read more →"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is Power Play?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Power Play is a free monthly global series hosted by Van. BOJA on Google Meet. It's a fierce monthly gathering for musicians, creatives, worship leaders and culture shapers. Register free →"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What age can students start?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"From age 4. Our youngest students follow an early-childhood program developing coordination, rhythm and a love for music through play-based learning."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I pay? Which methods do you accept?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Through the apply page you can pay securely via Paystack (cards, bank, USSD, QR, mobile money), Flutterwave (cards, M-Pesa, Apple/Google Pay), Stripe (international cards), or bank transfer. All transactions are encrypted; we never see your card details."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need to own an instrument?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For in-person lessons we provide instruments during class for beginners. We strongly recommend home practice and can advise on affordable instruments within your budget."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many lessons per week?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most programmes are one 60-minute lesson per week. Theory classes are twice weekly. We recommend 20–30 minutes of daily home practice for optimal progress."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are weekend classes available?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. We offer both weekday and weekend slots. Saturday morning sessions are particularly popular for school-age students and working adults."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What's the connection between MAM Academy and MAM Centre?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"MAM Academy is the training arm of MAM Centre — A Centre for Honourable Music, Arts & Formation. The ecosystem also includes MAM Auditer (assessment platform) and FH-MAM (Fellowship for Honourable Musicians)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I pause or cancel my enrollment?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You may pause for up to 4 weeks per term and we hold your seat. For cancellations, give at least 2 weeks' notice before the next billing date. Email academy@mamcentre.org."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a performance or recital at the end of term?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes — each term ends in a student showcase. Stage experience is essential to formation, and parents, family and friends are warmly invited."}}]}</script>
