  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="faq-list">
        <article class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>What is MAM Auditer and why is it required?</span><span class="faq-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></span></button><div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">MAM Auditer is our structured entry assessment system. It measures 10 dimensions — rhythm intelligence, ear sensitivity, performance confidence, technical knowledge, artistic potential, discipline and learning capacity — so we place you in the right pathway from day one. Students are not randomly placed; they are intelligently assessed.</div></div></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>Can I study online or do I have to come to Lagos?</span><span class="faq-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></span></button><div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">All MAM programmes are offered in two modes. <strong>Online:</strong> live video classes, online coaching, digital assignments, virtual rehearsals — from anywhere. <strong>Onsite:</strong> in-person at MAM Centre, Lagos — for practical rehearsals, ensemble training, live stagecraft and group interactions.</div></div></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>How are MAM certifications equivalent to Trinity London?</span><span class="faq-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></span></button><div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Our four pathways map directly to Trinity College London grade bands: Pre-Certification (Grade 1–2), Certification (Grade 3–4), Pre-Diploma (Grade 5–6) and Diploma (Grade 7–8). Plus the MAM Method adds rhythm intelligence, performance intelligence and creative consciousness on top.</div></div></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>What does each pathway cost?</span><span class="faq-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></span></button><div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Certified Musician from <span data-amt-usd="240">$240</span> (one tradition) · Grand Musician from <span data-amt-usd="313">$313</span> (all three traditions, 13% off), both spanning all four certification levels and available online or onsite. Registration is <span data-amt-usd="5">$5</span> (one-time). Crash Programmes are a flat <span data-amt-usd="70">$70</span> for a 6-week accelerated intensive. The MetaMusic Order (12 weeks) is <span data-amt-usd="60">$60</span>.</div></div></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>What is The MetaMusic Order?</span><span class="faq-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></span></button><div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">A 12-week civilization-engineering intensive that moves musicians from <em>Performer</em> → <em>Architect</em>. It immerses students in sound psychology, cultural engineering, atmosphere architecture, performance intelligence and national responsibility. <a href="metamusic-order">Read more →</a></div></div></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>What is Power Play?</span><span class="faq-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></span></button><div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Power Play is a <strong>free</strong> monthly global series hosted by Van. BOJA on Google Meet. It's a fierce monthly gathering for musicians, creatives, worship leaders and culture shapers. <a href="power-play">Register free →</a></div></div></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>What age can students start?</span><span class="faq-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></span></button><div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">From age 4. Our youngest students follow an early-childhood program developing coordination, rhythm and a love for music through play-based learning.</div></div></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>How do I pay? Which methods do you accept?</span><span class="faq-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></span></button><div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Through the apply page you can pay securely via <strong>Paystack</strong> (cards, bank, USSD, QR, mobile money), <strong>Flutterwave</strong> (cards, M-Pesa, Apple/Google Pay), <strong>Stripe</strong> (international cards), or <strong>bank transfer</strong>. All transactions are encrypted; we never see your card details.</div></div></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>Do I need to own an instrument?</span><span class="faq-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></span></button><div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">For in-person lessons we provide instruments during class for beginners. We strongly recommend home practice and can advise on affordable instruments within your budget.</div></div></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>How many lessons per week?</span><span class="faq-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></span></button><div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Most programmes are one 60-minute lesson per week. Theory classes are twice weekly. We recommend 20–30 minutes of daily home practice for optimal progress.</div></div></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>Are weekend classes available?</span><span class="faq-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></span></button><div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes. We offer both weekday and weekend slots. Saturday morning sessions are particularly popular for school-age students and working adults.</div></div></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>What's the connection between MAM Academy and MAM Centre?</span><span class="faq-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></span></button><div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">MAM Academy is the training arm of MAM Centre — A Centre for Honourable Music, Arts &amp; Formation. The ecosystem also includes MAM Auditer (assessment platform) and FH-MAM (Fellowship for Honourable Musicians).</div></div></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>Can I pause or cancel my enrollment?</span><span class="faq-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></span></button><div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">You may pause for up to 4 weeks per term and we hold your seat. For cancellations, give at least 2 weeks' notice before the next billing date. Email <a href="mailto:academy@mamcentre.org">academy@mamcentre.org</a>.</div></div></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false"><span>Is there a performance or recital at the end of term?</span><span class="faq-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></span></button><div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes — each term ends in a student showcase. Stage experience is essential to formation, and parents, family and friends are warmly invited.</div></div></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

